{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ML8vW8q3tjWRQXmZMmThmN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both reviewers completed independently. Now conducting the roundtable synthesis (Steps 2-4).\n\n**Step 2 — Cross-sharing summary:**\n- R1 (Methods+Experiments): Score 3, Confidence 4. Core concerns: n=5 statistical power, CSS wins only 2/5, k=75 degree of freedom, incomplete ablation robustness, method set confound.\n- R2 (Novelty+Related Work): Score 3, Confidence 4. Core concerns: CSS identical to feature selection stability index (unacknowledged), 14 references severely insufficient, no Mondorf et al. head-to-head, no size-controlled baselines, CIRCUS implementation validity.\n\n**Step 3 — Convergence:** Both reviewers agree on score (3) and share two key appraisals: (a) ACDC binarization pathology is the strongest contribution, (b) the Jaccard-utility claim is statistically underpowered. R2 raises a novelty concern (feature selection stability) that strengthens the case for Weak Reject. R1's experimental concerns about confounded cross-model comparison and k-sensitivity are complementary.\n\nNow producing the final synthesized report and submitting."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8941,"cache_read_input_tokens":59723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8941},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da6c2831-13c3-4ab7-a8ff-27a4cd9a02b2","uuid":"8fcc421f-d934-46ee-98a4-f5fb169f4776"}
